    <string name="privacy_title">Privacy policy</string>
    <string name="privacy_open">Read the privacy policy</string>
    <string name="privacy_updated">In effect since 6 September 2026</string>
    <string name="privacy_summary">In short: BrainXP keeps the material you hand in, your answers, and a record of your playtime. No ads, no trackers, and no data sold.</string>

    <string name="privacy_collect_heading">What we collect</string>
    <string name="privacy_collect_body">When you sign up: your email address, password, and the name you use inside the app. The password is stored scrambled, not as you typed it. If this phone was paired by a parent using a code, it sends no email or password at all — only the pairing code, the phone model, and an install marker.</string>

    <string name="privacy_apps_heading">Apps and time used</string>
    <string name="privacy_apps_body">The list of apps you lock is kept on the server so the rules are the same everywhere. While you are spending playtime, BrainXP sends the name of the app you opened and how many seconds went by, because that is how your balance is worked out. BrainXP reads which app is in front only while the screen is on, and apps you have not locked are never recorded anywhere.</string>

    <string name="privacy_material_heading">Material and answers</string>
    <string name="privacy_material_body">Photos of notes or files you hand in are sent to the server, because that is where the text is read and the questions are built. Your chosen answers and essay text are sent to be marked. BrainXP does not read file contents on your phone and never touches other photos in your gallery — only the ones you pick yourself.</string>

    <string name="privacy_accessibility_heading">Accessibility service</string>
    <string name="privacy_accessibility_body">This is a choice, not a requirement, and skipping it costs you nothing. If you turn it on, BrainXP receives only the package name of the app that just came to the front, so blocking happens sooner. BrainXP does not read your screen, does not read what you type, and records nothing from other apps.</string>

    <string name="privacy_family_heading">Family Mode</string>
    <string name="privacy_family_body">In Family Mode, a parent sees the school level, the material handed in, session results, and playtime used. The parent is also told when protection on the child\' phone stops working or a permission is revoked. The parent does not see the contents of the notes the child photographed, and does not see other apps used beyond the locked ones.</string>

    <string name="privacy_share_heading">We do not share it</string>
    <string name="privacy_share_body">No data is sold or traded. BrainXP carries no ads, no analytics tooling, and no third-party crash reporting. Data moves only between your phone and the BrainXP server, always over an encrypted connection.</string>

    <string name="privacy_keep_heading">How long we keep it</string>
    <string name="privacy_keep_body">Material and history stay as long as your account exists, so you can reuse them. You can delete material one item at a time from your library whenever you like. What is on the phone is only a copy so the app keeps working without a signal, and it goes when the app is uninstalled.</string>

    <string name="privacy_delete_heading">Deleting your account</string>
    <string name="privacy_delete_body">You can ask for your account and all its data to be deleted from Settings, under Delete account. Requests are handled within 30 days, after which your material, history, balance, and profile are gone and cannot be brought back.</string>

    <string name="privacy_children_heading">Children</string>
    <string name="privacy_children_body">BrainXP is intended for ages 13 and over. Children under 13 should use BrainXP through Family Mode, paired by a parent with a code, because that route asks a child for no email, password, or name at all.</string>

    <string name="privacy_contact_heading">Contacting us</string>
    <string name="privacy_contact_body">For questions about your data, or to ask for your account to be deleted, write to dukungan@satu-miliar-pertama-di-2027.biz.id.</string>
    <string name="privacy_contact_email">dukungan@satu-miliar-pertama-di-2027.biz.id</string>

